  "findings": [
    "Main.measure dispatches by mode and calls the real monotonic start before the selected worker; generator/initial owner setup is outside it.",
    "Main.finish optimized assembly calls real cinch_clock_monotonic_ns before examining ByteRun or loading its Bytes owner at offset16. Result-wrapper destruction, retained-byte reads and owner release therefore remain after the closing clock.",
    "All six workers use raw U32/U64 metadata and direct three-word aggregate worker returns; ByteRun construction is at the completed worker/wrapper boundary, not a new result tuple on each loop iteration. Public Result/UUID snapshots remain legitimate per-operation allocations.",
    "Counter worker optimizes to a register-only loop with no calls; it retains the checksum and count rather than becoming a constant.",
    "Random and UUID workers retain actual cinch_random_bytes calls in their operation paths; allocation worker retains cinch_bytes_new and changing cinch_bytes_set calls.",
    "Clock control retains the actual wall-clock operation; source Effect.Clock and actual runtime archive provider were qualified independently.",
    "Pure sample/validity arithmetic is allowed to optimize; native object/LLVM/assembly identities are fixed between the two linked runtime variants.",
    "Allocation statistics span the whole process, including post-clock variable-checksum decimal formatting; random output may change post-clock Nat/report allocation counts, so exact random whole-process counts are not forced equal."
  ],
